WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.480
When David Hyde Pierce confirmed that he wouldn't&nbsp;
be reprising his role on the rebooted "Frasier,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:10.560
fans were left wondering: What will happen&nbsp;
to Niles? Will he stay in Seattle? Or was he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:16.120
unceremoniously killed off? A recent episode&nbsp;
of the reboot finally gave us an answer.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:20.520
Fans of high-brow humor rejoiced when it was&nbsp;
announced that "Frasier" was coming back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:26.160
Paramount+. However, it wasn't all good news,&nbsp;
as it also came to light that David Hyde Pierce&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.000
would not reprise the part of Frasier's&nbsp;
brother, Niles, citing his desire not to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.240
repeat the same old roles. However, Niles is&nbsp;
still an integral component of this universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:40.568
so it only makes sense for the reboot to address&nbsp;
what happened to him and whether he's even alive.

00:00:40.568 --> 00:00:43.520
"Frasier" viewers can rest&nbsp;
easy. Niles is still alive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:48.760
so the chance of at least a cameo materializing&nbsp;
in the new show is still on the table. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:52.520
fans would be forgiven for wondering if&nbsp;
Niles bit the dust at some point because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:57.440
the reboot has kept mum on what exactly went&nbsp;
down between him and Frasier. The new season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:02.547
contains a moment when Olivia mentions a&nbsp;
sibling rivalry, to which Frasier responds:

00:01:02.547 --> 00:01:05.613
"I am familiar with the dynamic."

00:01:05.613 --> 00:01:09.840
Frasier's response could hint at the fact&nbsp;
that the two simply aren't on speaking terms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.480
which would explain why Niles isn't around&nbsp;
and why Frasier doesn't talk about him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:18.360
much. But seeing how Frasier spends time with&nbsp;
Niles' son, David, and David hasn't mentioned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:22.760
anything about his father passing away, it's&nbsp;
safe to say Niles is out there somewhere.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:27.280
Given his status as a beloved sitcom character,&nbsp;
it also makes sense that Niles wouldn't be killed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:31.520
off in the new "Frasier" series. While David&nbsp;
Hyde Pierce may not want to make a habit of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:36.840
returning to old roles, he may be up for a small&nbsp;
appearance down the line. After all, the original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:42.440
"Frasier" lasted for 11 seasons, so hopefully, the&nbsp;
revival will stick around for a while. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:47.800
in the universe of the show, it's kind of sad to&nbsp;
think that Frasier and Niles are no longer close.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:52.160
If Niles had died on "Frasier," the characters&nbsp;
could have moved on, but as it stands, there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:57.440
a huge hole missing on the rebooted series. And&nbsp;
now that Frasier is spending time with Niles' son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:01.600
it's even weirder if he never comes around.&nbsp;
The two could remain estranged within the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:05.760
series if Pierce is adamantly against&nbsp;
returning, which would be a sad end for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:11.040
the brothers. And it sort of shows how Frasier&nbsp;
can never make any familial relationships last.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:15.040
The revival sees him move to Boston, mostly&nbsp;
so that he can reconnect with his own son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.080
Freddy. Frasier never had a chance to get&nbsp;
close to him before, and it may have come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:22.800
at the expense of his relationship with&nbsp;
his brother taking a turn for the worse.

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:25.960
Of course, it would be incredibly&nbsp;
cathartic for fans to see Niles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:29.840
again. The show could address why things may&nbsp;
have turned frosty between the brothers and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.720
even see them reconcile. Niles doesn't&nbsp;
have to move to Boston with everyone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:38.102
but just one episode of Frasier and&nbsp;
Niles joking around would be delightful.

00:02:38.102 --> 00:02:42.320
However, if you miss seeing Pierce on&nbsp;
screen, he has a new series to watch.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:47.520
He stars as Paul Child in the series "Julia,"&nbsp;
streaming on Max. The 2022 drama covers the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:52.840
fruitful life of American celebrity chef, Julia&nbsp;
Child. Season 2 premiered in November 2023,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:57.160
but due to the ongoing SAG-AFTRA strike, you&nbsp;
likely haven't heard much about the series. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:01.920
now is a better time than ever to see how Pierce&nbsp;
portrays Julia's husband and creative partner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:05.289
as we wait to see what future&nbsp;
Niles has on the small screen.

